                    {
                        "sense_id": "298c7a62-ba64-3f0f-a612-68a98a6110b2",
                        "entry_id": "4055fddd-3016-3fdb-96bc-6f5682a0a55f",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Synonym of Jacobin, of, related to, or characteristic of the Jacobins of France."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "historical"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "4a18293e-6038-4d50-8145-9edfa4bbe969",
                                "sense_id": "298c7a62-ba64-3f0f-a612-68a98a6110b2",
                                "text": "1793, Edmund Burke, “Remarks on the Policy of the Allies with Respect to France” in Three memorials on French affairs, London: F. & C. Rivington, 1797,\nHer late dangers have arisen […] from her own ill policy, which dismantled all her towns, and discontented all her subjects by Jacobinical innovations."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "7822de95-39f5-494c-a17c-1a86640f1b7a",
                                "sense_id": "298c7a62-ba64-3f0f-a612-68a98a6110b2",
                                "text": "1834, Samuel Taylor Coleridge, “A Character,” lines 49-52, in Ernest Hartley Coleridge (ed.), Coleridge: Poetical Works, Oxford University Press, 1912, p. 452,\nAnd though he never left in lurch\nHis King, his country, or his church,\n’Twas but to humour his own cynical\nContempt of doctrines Jacobinical."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "09369011-da7e-42b2-84e8-41e7c23c8fca",
                                "sense_id": "298c7a62-ba64-3f0f-a612-68a98a6110b2",
                                "text": "She is always ready for jacobinical scoffs at a man for being a lord, if he happens to fail; she is always ready for toadying a lord, if he happens to make a hit."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "544f7c91-8c8f-4486-bb28-8ec7b56fc5fd",
                                "sense_id": "298c7a62-ba64-3f0f-a612-68a98a6110b2",
                                "text": "“And there must be no letter-scribbling to your cousin Hortense: no intercourse whatever. I do not approve of the principles of the family; they are Jacobinical.”"
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
